or inference and serving stacks. Overall, uplift is jagged, and humans rema=
in a core part of the AI research loop.</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p:only-of-type]:mb-0"><strong>Agent use is surg=
ing, and the heaviest users are pulling further ahead.</strong> At API list=
 prices, the median researcher=E2=80=99s daily usage reached $2,400 in Octo=
ber, up 62% from September. At the 90th percentile it reached $23,000, up 1=
05% from September. A survey gives us another indication of how much resear=
chers value these tools. Asked what they would trade to keep frontier codin=
g agents for three months, the median answers were 30% of team compute or, =
in a separate question, 40% of team headcount.</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p:only-of-type]:mb-0"><strong>Researchers are d=
evoting increasing human effort to Safety and Alignment</strong>, which saw=
 the largest absolute increase in documented research efforts across all of=
 OpenAI=E2=80=99s major research areas. Safety and Alignment=E2=80=99s docu=
mented workweeks increased by 77% from January to September due to both new=
