toc-button-h)+var(--anchor-scroll-clearance))]">Where researchers allocate =
their time</h3></div>
<div class=3D"col-span-full toc-visible:@md:col-start-2 @md:col-span-6 @md:=
col-start-4 max-w-none min-w-0 in-[:where(li)]:contents not-first:mt-6"><p =
class=3D"mb-(--prose-body-margin-bottom,--spacing(6)) last:mb-0">Finally, w=
e examine how researchers allocate their time across research areas. We fir=
st collected individual-level contributions from researchers in the form of=
 company-public Slack posts, pull requests, and internal documents from Jan=
uary through September 2026. We then used classifiers to group these contri=
butions into research areas, and each researcher-week was divided equally a=
cross that researcher=E2=80=99s verified projects for the week. This provid=
es a proxy for where researchers were directing their attention.</p></div>
<div class=3D"col-span-full toc-visible:@md:col-start-2 @md:col-span-6 @md:=
col-start-4 max-w-none min-w-0 in-[:where(li)]:contents not-first:mt-6"><p =
class=3D"mb-(--prose-body-margin-bottom,--spacing(6)) last:mb-0">Importantl=
y, unlike our other analyses, <strong>the =E2=80=9Cresearch area=E2=80=9D w=
e classify here does not correspond to formal reporting lines</strong>. For=
 example, a researcher on a posttraining team who spends half their time on=
 infrastructure improvements would be estimated as contributing half a work=
week to Scaling / Infrastructure Contributions and half to Posttraining Con=
tributions. This allows us to create a robust measurement of where research=
ers are actively spending time even if they do not formally shift teams.</p=
></div>
<div class=3D"col-span-full toc-visible:@md:col-start-2 @md:col-span-6 @md:=
col-start-4 max-w-none min-w-0 in-[:where(li)]:contents not-first:mt-6"><p =
class=3D"mb-(--prose-body-margin-bottom,--spacing(6)) last:mb-0">We find th=
at the amount of researcher time dedicated to each of the areas we identify=
 has grown over the course of 2026. Notably, using this methodology, we fin=
d that Safety &amp; Alignment saw the largest absolute increase across any =
research area, almost doubling in documented workweek contributions since t=
he start of the year due to a combination of new hires and existing researc=
hers shifting their focus toward safety projects. This research area covers=
 workstreams such as alignment evals, monitorability, and reward hacking re=
search. A notable inflection point that we measure in the growth of Safety =
&amp; Alignment coincides with the aftermath of the <a class=3D"transition =
ease-curve-a duration-250 text-primary-100 hover:text-primary-60 underline-=
offset-[0.25rem] decoration-1 underline relative" data-analytics=3D"mdx-bod=
y-link" href=3D"https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-model-evaluation-secu=
rity-incident/">Hugging Face incident<!-- -->=E2=81=A0</a> in July, and Ope=
nAI=E2=80=99s subsequent work to <a class=3D"transition ease-curve-a durati=
on-250 text-primary-100 hover:text-primary-60 underline-offset-[0.25rem] de=
coration-1 underline relative" data-analytics=3D"mdx-body-link" href=3D"htt=
ps://openai.com/index/towards-safety-cases-for-frontier-ai-training/">devel=
op and improve safety cases for frontier AI training<!-- -->=E2=81=A0</a>.<=
/p></div>
<div class=3D"col-span-full toc-visible:@md:col-start-2 @md:col-span-6 @md:=
col-start-4 max-w-none min-w-0 in-[:where(li)]:contents not-first:mt-6"><p =
class=3D"mb-(--prose-body-margin-bottom,--spacing(6)) last:mb-0">We note th=
at the distinction between research areas, and especially posttraining vers=
us safety and alignment, is nontrivial and we may iterate on the definition=
 over time. The methods section below describes examples of high-level work=
streams.</p></div>
