class=3D"mb-(--prose-body-margin-bottom,--spacing(6)) last:mb-0">To better =
understand how agent use might affect research productivity, we next examin=
e how the process of conducting AI research at OpenAI is changing. The prod=
uctivity gains from new technologies depend in part on how work is reorgani=
zed around them. As agents improve, researchers may change which tasks they=
 delegate to AI, how they oversee and coordinate agents=E2=80=99 work, and =
which projects they pursue. Below, we report both quantitative and qualitat=
ive measures of how AI is changing the process of conducting AI research at=
 OpenAI. Together, these different types of data contribute to a (partial) =
view of how researchers are reorganizing their work around agents and how r=
esearchers remain in the loop today.</p></div>
